  "generatedAt": "2026-09-25",
  "commits": [
    "8a2795a2 Play HMH SFX through Web Audio buffers and retire footstep cues",
    "17728eb0 Count SFX voices in the HMH crowd bench and unlock audio in the leak probe"
  ],
  "base": "839358b6 (step 4 evidence; runtime code identical to c85b2d89)",
  "deviceAcceptance": false,
  "note": "Chrome CPU-throttle proxy for an iPhone XS Max (414x896 @3, mobile profile); GPU work is not throttled and no iOS hardware was used. Other sessions kept the host 25-60% busy, so the step-4 build (.tmp/step5/dist-step4, a --sourcemap build of HEAD, byte-identical to .tmp/step4/dist-final) and this build (.tmp/step5/dist-final) were alternated in two rounds with the same bench script. Rows with loadMatched:false drew host-load windows more than ~3 points apart or above 33% other load; they are reported but left out of the summary. Both builds play the same cue stream: 344-366 cue voices started per 20 s window.",
  "change": [
    "apps/hmh-reboot/src/combat-audio.mjs: every SFX cue used to be a new HTMLAudioElement(url). Now one AudioContext is created in the first gesture; each sample a cue can reach in the mode is fetched and decoded once (4 at a time) into an AudioBuffer; a cue is AudioBufferSourceNode -> per-voice GainNode (cue plan volume x boss duck) -> SFX or UI bus GainNode (slider level x dynamic range) -> destination. Registry gate, cooldowns, the 16-voice cap, priority stealing, 4 s reaping, the 600 ms boss duck (x0.7; boss, damage and ui exempt), the pause allow-list and reduce-motion attenuation are unchanged. Standalone music is still a media element; embedded music stays with the parent player.",
    "Gestures: pointerdown, pointerup, touchend and keydown (capture, passive) stay attached. The first unlocks: resume() and a one-sample buffer inside the gesture, as iOS requires (a touch pointerdown is not an activation there). Later ones resume a context iOS interrupted. visibilitychange suspends the context when hidden and resumes it when visible. destroy() closes the context and removes every listener. main.mjs passes gestureTarget: window and visibilityTarget: document and drops its once-only pointerdown/keydown unlock.",
    "Cues are dropped, not played late, while the context is locked or suspended or while a sample is still decoding; a requested sample jumps the decode queue. A failed fetch or decode makes that cue silent (sample-unavailable) without leaking a voice.",
    "Owner decision: no footsteps and no voice lines. footstep-dirt and footstep-road are refused in every mode (cue-retired) and never fetched; the unused worldDesignFootstep selector is removed. No voice-line cue exists in the child.",
    "Telemetry adds audioContext, audioSamplesReady and audioSamplesFailed. The crowd bench counts media-element plays, buffer-source starts and SFX requests in each window. The leak probe gives each mounted child one trusted key press. The weapon SFX smoke presses Shift and asserts a running context and zero failed samples."
  ],
