  "exactness": {
    "gainParity": "scripts/hmh-action-audio-audit.mjs run through the 1.8.1-era engine (HTMLAudioElement probe) and through this engine (fake Web Audio graph): the routed gain of all 35 live manifest cues is bit-identical, and the synthetic 154-event dense combat mix WAV and the audition WAV are byte-identical. The two footstep cues are now listed as retiredFromPlayback.",
    "unitTests": "tests/hmh-reboot-combat-audio-webaudio.test.mjs has 17 tests; 16 were red before the change. It covers: no per-cue media element; nothing fetched before a gesture, then each sample exactly once; footsteps retired in every mode; cues dropped while decoding; live SFX/UI bus gain (the iOS volume fix); the 16-voice cap; the boss duck window; visibility suspend/resume; interruption recovery on the next touch; pointerup/touchend/keydown unlock; ended-voice release; failed fetch/decode; no Web Audio; destroy; the pause-menu preview; every weapon cue. The four suites that drove an HTMLAudioElement fake (combat-audio, combat-audio-routing, action-sfx, objective-audio) now drive tests/helpers/fake-web-audio.mjs with the same assertions on source buffers and graph gain.",
