    "finding": "Renderer private memory grows about the same with either engine over 21,600 ticks (step 4: 371.8 -> 435.6 MB, +63.8 MB; this build: 367.0 -> 432.8 MB, +65.8 MB) while the retained JS heap stays at 16-18 MB. Per-cue HTMLAudioElements were one of the two candidates step 4 named for that growth; they are not the cause. The decoded SFX buffers are about 3.5 MB (35 mono samples, about 18 s of audio at 48 kHz float)."
  },
  "cleanupList": [
    "apps/portal/assets/audio/sfx/hmh-footstep-dirt.wav and hmh-footstep-road.wav are unreachable from playback. They stay because the portal-owned apps/portal/assets/audio/sfx/hmh-weapon-sfx-manifest.json still lists them, and tests/hmh-reboot-action-sfx.test.mjs checks every manifest file on disk.",
    "apps/portal/src/hmh-audio-system.mjs still registers footstep-dirt and footstep-road (portal-owned).",
    "scripts/build-hmh-weapon-sfx.py still synthesises hmh-footstep-dirt and hmh-footstep-road; change it together with the manifest.",
    "docs/qa/hmh-action-audio-20260911.json, docs/qa/hmh-frontier-action-audio-20260911.json and docs/audio/hard-money-heroes-audio-*.json mention the footstep cues as history.",
    "weapon-fire (weapon-fire.ogg) is registered and preloaded in gameplay mode, but main.mjs never plays it (each weapon has its own hmh-fire-* cue)."
  ],
  "deferred": [
    "No iOS hardware test: unlock on the Enter tap, resume after a call or Siri interruption, and the ring/silent switch. With navigator.audioSession left at its default, WebKit may treat Web Audio SFX as ambient and mute them with the silent switch while the parent music keeps playing. Setting navigator.audioSession.type = \"playback\" would make SFX ignore the switch; that is an owner call.",
    "Renderer private memory growth (+64-66 MB over 21,600 ticks) remains; decoded images and GPU-side resources are the remaining candidates.",
    "Owner target: at 4x this build averages about 48 fps (20.3-21.1 ms, 1.7-4.7% of frames over 33.3 ms); at 6x it is about 20-21 fps (47-50 ms), still below 30."
  ],
